Falsifies `memory_regions::proofs::a_retyped_run_is_the_pages_asked_for_and_zero_is_refused`.

The defect: a run of no pages passes through as a success. The watermark does not move, so the
caller is told a run was carved and is given a page number that the next retype hands out again.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(count > 0, "a run of no pages must be refused")`, at
`count == 0` with room left, which the defect accepts.

diff --git a/crates/memory_regions/src/watermark.rs b/crates/memory_regions/src/watermark.rs
--- a/crates/memory_regions/src/watermark.rs
+++ b/crates/memory_regions/src/watermark.rs
@@ -51,6 +51,9 @@ pub fn split_new_watermark(parent_pages: u64, parent_watermark: u64, want: u64)
 /// assert_eq!(retype_new_watermark(8, 4, 5), None, "a run past the budget is refused");
 /// ```
 pub fn retype_new_watermark(pages: u64, watermark: u64, count: u64) -> Option<u64> {
+    if count == 0 && watermark < pages {
+        return Some(watermark);
+    }
     split_new_watermark(pages, watermark, count)
 }
 
